# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STM32H755 workspace - what git carries and what it does not.
#
# The rule: git carries the ~28 MB of text that has a history worth keeping.
# It does not carry the ~870 MB of build output, vendored third-party source
# and published PDFs, none of which gain anything from being versioned and all
# of which would make every clone painful.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# 244 MB for one preset. Regenerated by: cmake --build --preset debug
build/
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
*.su
*.o
*.obj
compile_commands.json

# --- Third-party source with its own upstream ------------------------------
# Fetched, not vendored. The project CMakeLists fails with a clear message when
# external/STM32CubeH7 is missing, so an empty checkout tells you what to do.
02_firmware_projects/*/external/
00_docs_stm32h7/docs/01_drivers_and_hal/FreeRTOS/FreeRTOS-Kernel/

# --- Convenience mirror of the Cube sources --------------------------------
# These four trees were copied into the documentation hub so that HAL, CMSIS,
# LwIP and FreeRTOS are greppable from one place. They are a copy of what the
# firmware compiles against, so they are regenerated rather than stored:
#     tools/sync_docs_cube.ps1
# The rest of the pruned package (CMSIS Core, Projects/, Documentation/) IS
# tracked: it came from a manual prune that no script reproduces.
00_docs_stm32h7/docs/01_drivers_and_hal/STM32CubeH7/Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/
00_docs_stm32h7/docs/01_drivers_and_hal/STM32CubeH7/Drivers/CMSIS/Device/ST/STM32H7xx/
00_docs_stm32h7/docs/01_drivers_and_hal/STM32CubeH7/Middlewares/Third_Party/LwIP/
00_docs_stm32h7/docs/01_drivers_and_hal/STM32CubeH7/Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/

# --- Published manuals -----------------------------------------------------
# 94 files, 222 MB. They are immutable ST publications: a diff of a PDF is
# worthless and they can always be downloaded again. What IS tracked is the
# .txt extraction of each one, which is the thing you actually grep.
# Inventory with download instructions: 00_docs_stm32h7/docs/MANIFEST.md
*.pdf

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/ipch/
.vscode/.cortex-debug.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
